{{!-- One move row: the rollable <li> wrapper + the shared move-item body. Shared by the steading's
      rail (steading-move-panel), the rows a choice grants and the major-arcana card (arcanum-cards) so the
      roll wiring stays identical — a
      rollable move gets `.item[data-item-id]` so the sheet's roll handler resolves the OWNED move item
      (full description + 10+/7-9/6- result tiers) instead of a bare stat roll. Context is a MoveSnapshot;
      params: categoryKey, alwaysShowResource, disclosure, startOpen (forwarded to move-item). `is-open` is the row half of a disclosure's state — Disclosure toggles it there, so
      a row the template ships OPEN has to say so itself. `stonetop-item--nameless` says the row draws
      no name line, so its controls belong on the move's own first line instead — see the CSS. A
      disclosure row is never that: there the name IS the control that opens the text. --}}
{{#if rollStat}}
<li class="item stonetop-item{{#if (and nameless (not disclosure))}} stonetop-item--nameless{{/if}}{{#if startOpen}} is-open{{/if}}" data-disclosure-row data-item-id="{{ownedId}}">
{{else}}
<li class="stonetop-item{{#if (and nameless (not disclosure))}} stonetop-item--nameless{{/if}}{{#if startOpen}} is-open{{/if}}" data-disclosure-row>
{{/if}}
	{{> "stonetop.move-item" categoryKey=categoryKey alwaysShowResource=alwaysShowResource disclosure=disclosure startOpen=startOpen}}
</li>
